<div class="mw-parser-output"><h1>Level</h1>
<p>Syntax: 
</p>
<pre> level [now]
</pre>
<p>The level command is used to raise a level. This is because the training system keeps track of how many times you practice per level. When you issue the level command you raise a level, gain your ability and skill points, and can start a new (cheap) training session.
</p><p>Remember that each time you practice a certain skills/spells/abilities on a level it becomes more expensive to practice that same skill again. Until you raise a level. Thus it is to your advantage to raise one level at a time and practice before you raise the next. The <b>level now</b> command is used to raise a level even if you haven't trained your skills. You probably shouldn't do that.
</p><p>Experience is usually gained by killing monsters. The experience you gain is relative to your level compared to the monster's level.
</p><p>You gain no experience when killing players.
</p><p>If you are good and kill evil you get a bonus. Vice versa but not as large.
</p><p>You start at level 1 with 500 experience points. The table shows how many more you need for each level, and the total you need to have:
</p>
